{meta: tag kinderlied}
{key: Em}

{start_of_verse}
[Em]Old King [Am6]Cole was a [B]merry old soul
[B7]and a merry [Em]old [B]soul [Em]was [Am]he[B]
[Em]He called for his [Am6]pipes
[B7]and he called [Em]for his [Am6]bowl
[Em]and he [C]called for [Am]his [B7]fiddlers [Em]three
Every [Am]fiddler [F#7]had [B]a fine fiddle
[B7]And a [Em]very fine fiddle [C]had [B]he
[Em]Tweedle [Am6]dee, [B7]Tweedle dee, [Em]Tweedle dee, Tweedle [Am6]dee,
With [Em]king [C]Cole and his [Am]fid[B7]dlers [Em]three
{end_of_verse}
